index 0000000..4ec34d6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/member-bound-events.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Member-bound HTTP publication (proposal)
+
+`POST /events/member-bound` accepts only signed kind-9 channel messages. The
+request uses the existing event JSON and NIP-98 authorization format. The NIP-98
+`u` tag must name this exact route on the tenant host, and its payload digest
+must cover the event body. Dev `X-Pubkey` authentication is not accepted.
+
+The relay accepts only while the event signer has an active membership in the
+event's channel. The check uses the authoritative database, after acquiring the
+same per-community, per-channel advisory transaction lock as member removal.
+The event, thread metadata, and membership decision commit in one transaction.
+An absent, removed, or cross-community membership rejects with HTTP 400 and no
+event is stored. A duplicate event submitted after removal is also rejected.
+
+This distinct path is the capability check: older relays lack the route and
+cannot silently ignore an optional request header. Clients requiring the
+membership guarantee must send only to this path and require the exact event-ID
+acceptance response. `POST /events` keeps its current open-channel behavior.
+
+The guarantee orders the write against add/remove membership operations that
+use the channel-membership lock. A subsequent removal does not retract an event
+that committed first. Channel deletion uses a separate write path and is not
+serialized by this membership fence; its existing event-write guards still
+apply. This route does not assert that an ACP turn succeeded or that delivery
+to subscribers completed.
